<section class="wrap narrow section prose">
  <h1>Renting safely in Accra</h1>
  <p class="lead">Rental scams are common. These simple rules protect you, whether you find a place here or anywhere else.</p>

  <h2>Before you pay anything</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>View the property in person.</strong> Never send money (MoMo or bank) to “hold” a place you haven't seen.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm who owns it.</strong> Ask to see the title / indenture, a recent property-rate or ECG bill in the owner's name, and the landlord's Ghana Card. If someone is letting on the owner's behalf, ask for the owner's written authorisation and speak to the owner yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Talk to current tenants or neighbours</strong> about water, power and how the landlord treats tenants.</li>
    <li><strong>Prefer verified landlords.</strong> The ✔ badge means we've checked their Ghana Card. It is not a guarantee of the property, so still do the checks above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Know the law</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Under the <strong>Rent Act, 1963 (Act 220)</strong>, a landlord should not demand more than <strong>six months' advance</strong> rent.</li>
    <li>You're entitled to a <strong>written receipt</strong> (or rent card) for every payment.</li>
    <li>Disputes about rent, eviction or deposits can be taken to the <strong>Rent Control Department</strong> — there are Rent Offices across Greater Accra.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Signing the agreement</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Get a written tenancy agreement that states the rent, advance paid, duration, who pays utilities and how the deposit is returned.</li>
    <li>Pay to an account or MoMo number in the <strong>owner's name</strong>, and keep the reference.</li>
    <li>Do a walk-through and take dated photos of the condition of the property before moving in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Red flags</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The “landlord” is abroad and wants you to pay before seeing the place.</li>
    <li>A price far below similar homes in the same area.</li>
    <li>Requests for “viewing fees”, “form fees” or “agent fees”.</li>
    <li>Pressure to pay today because “many people are interested”.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>See something suspicious? Use <strong>🚩 Report this listing</strong> on the listing page, or email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. If you've lost money, report it to the Ghana Police Service.</p>
</section>
